    "finding": "Comparable on explicitly stated period, metric and units: both tracker documents specify calendar-2026 NVIDIA Data Center revenue in dollar billions, and current_view/Consensus already adopts $376bn. This is a provided fictional benchmark, not an independently audited compilation; the legacy 2024 label is stale. The broker’s own estimate is $385bn, raised from $370bn, with only capex above guide midpoints cited. No additional broker model was found. At our other inputs, $385bn can be reproduced by total capex $701.417bn (+$18.917bn), mix 39.0533%, NVIDIA spend share 66.8016%, or Big Four concentration 43.7864%, each separately; these are arithmetic alternatives, not attributed broker assumptions. compute verified each without saving. At our Q3 $103bn and monthly bridge, required Q4 is $145.4395bn for broker $385bn, $131.9395bn for tracker $376bn, and $129.8645bn for our base. A hypothetical Q3 $108bn instead would require $137.9395bn Q4 for $385bn. Retain inputs; actual broker attribution and tracker methodology remain unresolved.",
